    <node id="PHYSICAL EXAM">
      <data key="d0">PHYSICAL EXAM</data>
      <data key="d1">PHYSICAL EXAM</data>
      <data key="d2">endpoint</data>
      <data key="d3">A physical exam is a clinical evaluation conducted by a health care provider to assess the body for signs of disease or abnormality. It is a hands-on examination that typically checks vital signs—such as blood pressure, heart rate, and temperature—along with height, weight, and overall body condition. The provider systematically examines the heart, lungs, organs, lymph nodes, skin, eyes, ears, nose, throat, head, and neck. In some cases, the exam may include palpation of the oral cavity or the use of a mirror or fiberoptic scope to visualize hard-to-see areas. Depending on the clinical context, a physical exam may also involve checking the breasts, spleen, or liver.

This examination serves as a general health test and is often integrated into specific medical workflows. For example, it is part of the diagnostic evaluation for basal cell skin cancer and is listed as a testing component for ductal carcinoma in situ (DCIS) and treatment planning. In oncology, it is performed by specialists such as hematologists/oncologists, who may also assess the spleen and liver. For patients who have undergone a total thyroidectomy, a physical exam is part of short-term follow-up care. It is also a component of surveillance for stage 2 and 3 colon cancer, where it helps detect possible signs of recurrence; suspicious findings may prompt further imaging or blood tests. Additionally, after chemoradiation for certain cancers, the physical exam is often combined with digital rectal examination and anoscopy. In all settings, the physical exam provides a foundational, non-invasive method for identifying abnormalities, guiding further diagnostic steps, and monitoring patient health over time.
Relationships:
  - Source: HEALTH CARE PROVIDER
  - Target: PHYSICAL EXAM
  - Description: A health care provider is responsible for performing the physical exam, during which vital signs are also checked. The physical exam is carried out by the health care provider as part of the assessment process.
  - Source: PHYSICAL EXAM
  - Target: HEALTH CARE PROVIDER
  - Description: A health care provider may perform a physical exam
  - Source: GENERAL HEALTH HISTORY
  - Target: PHYSICAL EXAM
  - Description: A physical exam is part of the general health history and physical exam assessment
  - Source: PHYSICAL EXAM
  - Target: MEDICAL HISTORY AND PHYSICAL EXAM (H&amp;P)
  - Description: The H&amp;P includes the physical exam component.

---</data>
    </node>
