  - Description: The National Comprehensive Cancer Network (NCCN) provides patient guidelines for breast cancer. These guidelines comprehensively cover breast cancer basics, including information on the disease itself, as well as guidance on testing and treatment planning. The NCCN's patient guidelines address the full spectrum of breast cancer, specifically including ductal carcinoma in situ (DCIS), invasive breast cancer, and metastatic breast cancer.</data>
