  - Description: BeTobaccoFree.gov and CDC.gov/tobacco are both online support websites designed to help individuals quit smoking or vaping. They are recommended smoking cessation support resources and are frequently listed together in guidance as trusted online options for quitting tobacco use. Both websites serve as accessible, evidence-based quit-smoking and quit-vaping support tools, often cited side by side for individuals seeking help with nicotine addiction.
  - Source: BETOBACCOFREE.GOV
  - Target: CANCER TREATMENT
  - Description: BeTobaccoFree.gov is an online resource to help quit tobacco use, which improves cancer treatment outcomes.
  - Source: BETOBACCOFREE.GOV
