    <node id="ADVANCED-STAGE PROSTATE CANCER">
      <data key="d0">ADVANCED-STAGE PROSTATE CANCER</data>
      <data key="d1">ADVANCED-STAGE PROSTATE CANCER</data>
      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">Advanced-stage prostate cancer is prostate cancer that has spread outside the prostate to other areas of the body, including lymph nodes, bones, liver, lungs, or other organs. It is also referred to as metastatic or distant metastatic prostate cancer. This condition encompasses both regional prostate cancer and metastatic prostate cancer. Advanced-stage prostate cancer is usually a lifelong disease; however, treatment can slow its progression and help manage the condition.
Relationships: (None listed in the provided data)</data>
