      <data key="d6">: Patients should report any symptoms they are experiencing. In the context of conditions like chronic lymphocytic leukemia (CLL), specific symptoms called "B symptoms" are documented, including fevers when not sick, night sweats that drench sheets, and unexpected weight loss [Data: Entities (476); Sources (30)].
</data>
