    <node id="TNM STAGING">
      <data key="d0">TNM STAGING</data>
      <data key="d1">TNM STAGING</data>
      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">TNM staging is a classification method that scores Tumor (T), Node (N), and Metastasis (M) to help assign a cancer stage.
Relationships:
  - Source: TNM STAGING
  - Target: CANCER STAGING
  - Description: Cancer staging uses TNM staging scores to assign a cancer stage.
  - Source: TNM STAGING
  - Target: METASTASIS
  - Description: Metastasis is one of the three components scored in TNM staging. TNM staging includes the M category to indicate whether cancer has metastasized.</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">ENTITY: TNM STAGING
Description: TNM staging is a classification method that scores Tumor (T), Node (N), and Metastasis (M) to help assign a cancer stage.
