    <node id="EBRT">
      <data key="d0">EBRT</data>
      <data key="d1">EBRT</data>
      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">EBRT, or external beam radiation therapy, is a local treatment for cancerous lesions that delivers radiation from outside the body to a targeted area, such as the pelvis or a larger field. It is commonly recommended after surgery for local or regional recurrence, often in combination with systemic therapy. Additionally, EBRT may be administered with platinum chemotherapy as part of chemoradiation, enhancing its therapeutic effect. This summary incorporates all provided descriptions, highlighting EBRT's role as a localized treatment, its use in postoperative care for recurrent disease, and its integration with systemic and chemotherapeutic approaches.
Relationships: None listed

---</data>
