      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">HPV refers to the common sexually transmitted infection with human papillomavirus; persistent infection with high-risk strains is the strongest risk factor for cervical cancer and can also cause other cancers and genital warts.
Relationships:
  - Source: HPV
  - Target: CERVICAL CANCER
  - Description: Long-term infection with high-risk HPV is the risk factor most strongly linked with cervical cancer.
  - Source: HPV
  - Target: HPV VACCINATION
  - Description: The HPV vaccine prevents new HPV infections.
  - Source: HPV
  - Target: CERVICAL INTRAEPITHELIAL NEOPLASIA (CIN)
  - Description: HPV infection causes abnormal cervical cell changes known as CIN or cervical dysplasia.</data>
