    <node id="MYCHART">
      <data key="d0">MYCHART</data>
      <data key="d1">MYCHART</data>
      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">MyChart is a patient portal and online electronic health record system that patients can set up to manage their healthcare. It provides secure access to test results, allows users to track appointments, and enables communication with their care team. Available as an account system when offered by a healthcare provider, MyChart serves as a centralized digital tool for patients to stay engaged with their health information and care coordination.
Relationships:
  - Source: MYCHART
  - Target: CARE TEAM
  - Description: MyChart is a patient portal that enables patients to communicate with their care team and track appointments. Through MyChart, patients can send messages to their care team; however, portal messages are not immediately seen by the care team, meaning there may be a delay in response. MyChart serves as the primary tool for patients to stay in contact with their care providers and manage their scheduled appointments.
  - Source: CARE TEAM
  - Target: MYCHART
  - Description: MyChart is a patient portal tool that helps individuals track their medical appointments and communicate with their care team. It serves as a digital connection between patients and the healthcare providers responsible for their treatment. Through MyChart, patients can manage appointment schedules and stay in contact with their care team, ensuring coordinated and informed care.
  - Source: MYCHART
  - Target: PATIENT
  - Description: MyChart is a patient portal that allows patients to access test results, track appointments, and communicate with their care team. A patient may set up MyChart specifically to track appointments and communicate with their care team, thereby gaining access to these features and maintaining ongoing engagement with their healthcare providers.
  - Source: TEST RESULTS
  - Target: MYCHART
  - Description: MyChart allows patients to access their test results.
  - Source: MYCHART
  - Target: APPOINTMENTS
  - Description: MyChart is a tool that helps the patient keep track of their appointments, providing a convenient way to manage and stay informed about scheduled visits.
  - Source: APPOINTMENTS
  - Target: MYCHART
  - Description: MyChart helps patients track their appointments.
  - Source: MYCHART
  - Target: PHYSICIAN
  - Description: MyChart (the patient portal) messages are not immediately seen by a physician. Because of this, any urgent concerns should not be sent through MyChart or portal messaging; instead, they should be called directly to triage. Physicians do not monitor MyChart messages in real time, so portal messaging is not appropriate for time-sensitive or urgent medical issues.
  - Source: MYCHART
  - Target: NURSE
  - Description: MyChart messages are not immediately seen by a nurse. Because portal messages are not monitored in real time, urgent concerns should not be sent through MyChart. Instead, patients should call triage directly for immediate assistance. This ensures that time-sensitive medical issues receive prompt attention.
  - Source: MYCHART
  - Target: PATIENT PORTAL
  - Description: MyChart is a specific patient portal/health record account.</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
