      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">STEREOTACTIC BODY RADIATION THERAPY (SBRT) is a special and highly specialized form of external beam radiation therapy. It is used to treat a limited number of small metastases in the body, often referred to as oligometastases, including tumors located in the liver, lungs, or bone. SBRT delivers very precise, high-dose radiation directly to the tumor while minimizing damage to surrounding healthy tissue. This approach is particularly valuable in metastatic cancer settings, such as metastatic cervical cancer, and is typically completed in five or fewer treatment sessions.
Relationships: (None listed in the provided data)

