Relationships: None listed

ENTITY: TUMOR TESTING
Description: Also called somatic testing, molecular tumor testing, or tumor profiling; analyzes tumor tissue, metastatic biopsies, or blood containing tumor DNA to identify molecular markers and mutations in DNA repair genes
Relationships:
  - Source: GENETIC TESTING
  - Target: TUMOR TESTING
  - Description: Tumor testing is one of the two basic types of genetic testing for prostate cancer care

ENTITY: MOLECULAR BIOMARKER TESTING
Description: A test performed on a biopsy sample to examine molecular components and determine whether prostate cancer is lower risk or higher risk; also called genomic testing, tumor profiling, or molecular tumor testing.
Relationships:
  - Source: GENETIC TEST
  - Target: MOLECULAR BIOMARKER TESTING
  - Description: Molecular biomarker testing is one of the two basic types of genetic tests used for prostate cancer care.

