**ENTITY: HEPATITIS C**
Description: Hepatitis C is a viral infection caused by the hepatitis C virus (HCV). It is known to cause chronic hepatitis, cirrhosis, liver failure, and liver cancer. In the context of chronic lymphocytic leukemia (CLL), hepatitis C is an infection that is specifically tested for before CLL treatment begins.
Relationships:
  - Source: HEPATITIS C
  - Target: HEPATITIS B AND C TEST
  - Description: The test checks for hepatitis C.
  - Source: HEPATITIS C
  - Target: LIVER CANCER
  - Description: Hepatitis C can cause liver cancer.
  - Source: CIRRHOSIS
  - Target: HEPATITIS C
  - Description: Hepatitis C virus or infection can cause cirrhosis.
  - Source: HEPATITIS
  - Target: HEPATITIS C
  - Description: Hepatitis C is one of the viruses that cause hepatitis.
  - Source: HEPATITIS C
  - Target: CHRONIC HEPATITIS
  - Description: Hepatitis C can cause chronic hepatitis.
  - Source: HEPATITIS C
  - Target: LIVER FAILURE
  - Description: Hepatitis C can cause liver failure.

