**ENTITY: BCR::ABL1-NEGATIVE OR BCR::ABL1-LIKE B-ALL**
Description: BCR::ABL1-negative or BCR::ABL1-like B-ALL is a subtype of B-cell acute lymphoblastic leukemia (B-ALL). It is recognized as the most common type of B-ALL. For this subtype, participation in a clinical trial is considered the preferred treatment approach.
Relationships:
  - Source: BCR::ABL1-POSITIVE B-ALL
  - Target: BCR::ABL1-NEGATIVE OR BCR::ABL1-LIKE B-ALL
  - Description: These are distinct B-ALL subtypes classified by BCR::ABL1 status and are discussed in separate chapters of the NCCN guidelines.

