  - Description: SURGERY and CLINICAL TRIALS are both recognized treatment approaches in oncology, applicable to different cancer types. According to the provided descriptions, surgery is a treatment option for thyroid cancer, and clinical trials are also listed as another treatment option for the same disease. Similarly, both surgery and clinical trials are identified as treatment options for squamous cell skin cancer. Thus, these two entities are consistently presented as parallel therapeutic avenues for both thyroid cancer and squamous cell skin cancer. No contradictions exist between the descriptions. The combined understanding is that SURGERY and CLINICAL TRIALS are each considered viable treatment modalities for thyroid cancer and squamous cell skin cancer, with clinical trials offering access to investigational or alternative approaches alongside standard surgical intervention.

