      <data key="d3">Total thyroidectomy is a surgical procedure that involves the complete removal of the entire thyroid gland. In addition to removing the thyroid, nearby lymph nodes may also be excised if they are known or suspected to contain cancer. This procedure is recommended under specific clinical circumstances, including for suspected follicular or oncocytic cancer that has grown beyond the thyroid gland, for tumors larger than 4 cm, or when a more invasive cancer is found during a lobectomy. By removing the entire gland and potentially affected lymph nodes, total thyroidectomy serves as a definitive treatment for these conditions.
Relationships: (None listed in the provided data)</data>
