    <node id="PET/CT">
      <data key="d0">PET/CT</data>
      <data key="d1">PET/CT</data>
      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">PET/CT is a combined imaging test that pairs positron emission tomography with computed tomography. It uses a sugar radiotracer to make cancer appear brighter in images, and as a more advanced imaging test, it can detect whether cancer has spread farther than the lymph nodes.
Relationships:
  - Source: POSITRON EMISSION TOMOGRAPHY (PET)
  - Target: PET/CT
  - Description: PET is the emission-imaging component of PET/CT; PET/CT combines PET with CT.
  - Source: IMAGING
  - Target: PET/CT
  - Description: IMAGING encompasses various techniques used to visualize internal structures and detect disease. Among these, PET/CT is a more advanced imaging test that may be needed to detect cancer spread farther than lymph nodes. PET/CT is an imaging test that combines positron emission tomography (PET) with computed tomography (CT), allowing for both functional and anatomical assessment in a single procedure.
  - Source: COMPUTED TOMOGRAPHY
  - Target: PET/CT
  - Description: CT is combined with PET in a PET/CT scan to produce detailed images.

---</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
