    <node id="BURKITT LYMPHOMA">
      <data key="d0">BURKITT LYMPHOMA</data>
      <data key="d1">BURKITT LYMPHOMA</data>
      <data key="d2">endpoint</data>
      <data key="d3">Burkitt lymphoma is a type of non-Hodgkin lymphoma. It is widely recognized as essentially the same disease as Burkitt leukemia, which is also referred to as mature B-cell acute lymphoblastic leukemia (ALL) or Burkitt leukemia/mature B-cell ALL. These terms describe the same underlying condition, with the distinction primarily based on the extent of bone marrow and blood involvement at presentation. Burkitt lymphoma is thus considered equivalent to Burkitt leukemia and mature B-cell ALL in clinical and pathological terms.
Relationships: (None listed in the provided data)</data>
    </node>
