ENTITY: ACUTE MYELOID LEUKEMIA
Description: AML is a leukemia in which abnormal changes stop immature white blood cells called myeloid blasts or myeloblasts from maturing, causing a buildup of blasts in the bone marrow and blood; diagnosis generally requires 20% or more myeloblasts
