ENTITY: GENETIC AND BIOMARKER TESTS
Description: Genetic and biomarker tests are laboratory tests used in the management of acute myeloid leukemia (AML). These tests are performed to learn about the specific subtype of AML a patient has, to identify targeted treatment options, and to help determine prognosis. By analyzing genetic and biomarker information, healthcare providers can better understand the characteristics of the disease and tailor therapeutic strategies accordingly.
