      <data key="d3">BCR::ABL1-positive B-ALL is a distinct subtype of B-cell acute lymphoblastic leukemia (B-ALL) characterized by the presence of the BCR::ABL1 gene. This gene produces the BCR::ABL protein, which drives the disease. Treatment for this subtype specifically aims to stop the activity of the BCR::ABL protein and typically involves an intensive combination of systemic therapies.
