ENTITY: GENETIC TEST
Description: A genetic test is a medical test used to identify abnormal changes, known as mutations, in genes. These changes can indicate an inherited risk for certain cancers, such as inherited cancer risk. In the context of prostate cancer care, genetic testing is divided into two basic types: germline testing and molecular biomarker testing. Germline testing looks for inherited gene mutations, while molecular biomarker testing analyzes the tumor itself to detect genetic alterations that can guide treatment decisions. Together, these approaches help assess cancer risk, prognosis, and potential targeted therapies.
