ENTITY: CANCER CARE TEAM
Description: The cancer care team is the patient's dedicated medical team responsible for guiding and managing cancer treatment. This team decides on the appropriate treatment plan, and as part of its comprehensive care, it performs pregnancy tests before starting any cancer treatment to ensure patient safety. The team also assesses fertility risks associated with the proposed treatment, offering referrals to address fertility preservation or related concerns. In addition, the cancer care team communicates important diagnoses to the patient, such as Richter transformation, ensuring that patients are fully informed about their condition. Overall, this team provides holistic cancer care, encompassing diagnosis, treatment planning, pre-treatment screening, fertility considerations, and ongoing communication throughout the patient's cancer journey.
