    <node id="EGG FREEZING">
      <data key="d0">EGG FREEZING</data>
      <data key="d1">EGG FREEZING</data>
      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">Egg freezing, also known medically as oocyte cryopreservation or oocyte preservation, is a fertility preservation method in which unfertilized eggs are removed from a woman’s ovaries, frozen, and stored for later use. This procedure allows individuals to preserve their reproductive potential by safeguarding eggs for future fertilization attempts, typically when they are not yet ready to conceive or when medical treatments may affect fertility.
Relationships:
  - Source: EGG FREEZING
  - Target: FERTILITY COUNSELING
  - Description: Fertility counseling discusses fertility preservation options, including egg freezing.
  - Source: EGG FREEZING
  - Target: SPERM BANKING
  - Description: Both sperm banking and egg freezing are described as fertility preservation options that store gametes for later use.
  - Source: EGG FREEZING
  - Target: OOCYTE CRYOPRESERVATION
  - Description: Egg freezing is the procedure whose medical term is oocyte cryopreservation; they refer to the same fertility preservation method.
  - Source: CERVICAL CANCER
  - Target: EGG FREEZING
  - Description: Egg freezing may be discussed to preserve fertility in cervical cancer patients
  - Source: EGG FREEZING
  - Target: SURROGACY
  - Description: Frozen eggs from egg freezing can be used in surrogacy</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
