    <node id="SEXUAL REPRODUCTION">
      <data key="d0">SEXUAL REPRODUCTION</data>
      <data key="d1">SEXUAL REPRODUCTION</data>
      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">Sexual reproduction is a biological process for which the female reproductive system is specialized. In this process, the ovaries produce eggs, which are essential for sexual reproduction. Furthermore, sexual reproduction requires both the eggs made by the ovaries and hormones, which play a key role in enabling the process. Thus, the female reproductive system, egg production, and hormonal regulation are all integral to sexual reproduction.  
Relationships:  
  - Source: PREGNANCY  
  - Target: SEXUAL REPRODUCTION  
  - Description: Ovaries make eggs needed for sexual reproduction, and pregnancy occurs when a fertilized egg develops in the uterus.  
  - Source: MENSTRUAL CYCLE  
  - Target: SEXUAL REPRODUCTION  
  - Description: The ovaries release hormones that affect the menstrual cycle in the context of sexual reproduction.  
  - Source: BIRTH  
  - Target: SEXUAL REPRODUCTION  
  - Description: The female reproductive system functions for sexual reproduction, and birth is the delivery process of a baby that developed in the uterus.</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
