    <node id="RELATIONSHIP: CT SCAN → BIOPSY">
      <data key="d0">RELATIONSHIP: CT SCAN → BIOPSY</data>
      <data key="d1">RELATIONSHIP: CT SCAN → BIOPSY</data>
      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">A CT scan (computed tomography) is a medical imaging technique that can reveal suspicious areas within the body. When such an area is identified, a biopsy may be needed to sample the tissue for diagnosis. In this context, CT can also be used to guide the biopsy procedure, helping clinicians precisely target the suspicious region. Together, CT scanning and biopsy are complementary: the CT scan locates and characterizes the area of concern, while the biopsy, often guided by CT, obtains a tissue sample for further analysis.</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
