      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">EXTERNAL BEAM RADIATION THERAPY (EBRT) is a form of radiation therapy used to treat cancer. It works by directing a beam of radiation at the tumor from a machine located outside the body. In this approach, the radiation is delivered externally, targeting cancerous cells while sparing surrounding healthy tissue as much as possible.
Relationships:
  - Source: EXTERNAL BEAM RADIATION THERAPY (EBRT)
  - Target: CHEMORADIATION
  - Description: Chemoradiation includes EBRT combined with chemotherapy
  - Source: EXTERNAL BEAM RADIATION THERAPY (EBRT)
  - Target: PLATINUM CHEMOTHERAPY
  - Description: Platinum chemotherapy may be given during the same time period as EBRT
  - Source: EXTERNAL BEAM RADIATION THERAPY (EBRT)
  - Target: VAGINAL BRACHYTHERAPY
  - Description: Vaginal brachytherapy may be given in addition to EBRT
  - Source: EXTERNAL BEAM RADIATION THERAPY (EBRT)
  - Target: CERVICAL CANCER
  - Description: EBRT is recommended after surgery for cervical cancers with risk factors
  - Source: EXTERNAL BEAM RADIATION THERAPY (EBRT)
  - Target: RADIATION THERAPY
  - Description: EBRT is a type of radiation therapy</data>
