      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">Radiation therapy for the eyes is a treatment method for primary CNS lymphoma in the eyes. It can be delivered by expanding WBRT to include the eyes or by focusing radiation only on the eyes at a lower dose, and it usually treats both eyes at the same time. Possible side effects include temporary or permanent vision problems and cataracts.
