    <node id="PELVIC EXAM">
      <data key="d0">PELVIC EXAM</data>
      <data key="d1">PELVIC EXAM</data>
      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">An exam of the ovaries, cervix, uterus, and vagina using a speculum to detect abnormal changes; it may include a Pap test and sometimes an endometrial biopsy.
Relationships:
  - Source: OVARIAN CANCER
  - Target: PELVIC EXAM
  - Description: The pelvic exam checks for abnormal changes in the ovaries and nearby reproductive organs that could indicate ovarian cancer.
  - Source: UTERINE CANCER
  - Target: PELVIC EXAM
  - Description: An endometrial biopsy performed during a pelvic exam can rule out uterine cancer.
  - Source: PELVIC EXAM
  - Target: ABDOMINAL AND PELVIC EXAM
  - Description: The pelvic exam is one component of the abdominal and pelvic exam.
  - Source: ABDOMINAL EXAM
  - Target: PELVIC EXAM
  - Description: Both are performed as part of the abdominal and pelvic exam to evaluate suspected ovarian cancer.
  - Source: CERVICAL CANCER
  - Target: PELVIC EXAM
  - Description: A Pap test performed during a pelvic exam can detect cervical cancer.
  - Source: PELVIC EXAM
  - Target: ENDOMETRIAL BIOPSY
  - Description: An endometrial biopsy may be part of the initial evaluation during the pelvic exam.
  - Source: PELVIC EXAM
  - Target: PAP TEST
  - Description: A sample of cells for the Pap test may be removed during the pelvic exam.
  - Source: PELVIC EXAM
  - Target: RECTOVAGINAL EXAM
  - Description: A rectovaginal exam may be done during the pelvic evaluation to check for cancer between the rectum and vagina.</data>
