      <data key="d11">DIAGNOSTIC TESTS encompass a broad category of medical assessments used to identify the presence or cause of a condition. Within this category, GENETIC TESTS are included as a specific subset. GENETIC TESTS are diagnostic tests that look for inherited mutations related to prostate cancer risk. Together, these entities describe the relationship between the broader diagnostic category and the specialized genetic testing used to assess inherited prostate cancer susceptibility.</data>
