    <edge source="NCCN" target="RICHTER TRANSFORMATION" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">NCCN</data>
      <data key="d8">RICHTER TRANSFORMATION</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">The NCCN (National Comprehensive Cancer Network) Guidelines for Patients describe Richter transformation as a possible complication of chronic lymphocytic leukemia (CLL) that can lead to more aggressive lymphomas. Additionally, the NCCN Guidelines for Patients address caring for Richter transformation as part of living with CLL/SLL (chronic lymphocytic leukemia/small lymphocytic lymphoma). Together, these descriptions indicate that Richter transformation is recognized by the NCCN as both a significant CLL complication and an important aspect of ongoing patient care and disease management within the broader context of CLL/SLL.</data>
      <data key="d12">RICHTER TRANSFORMATION</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NCCN" target="CLINICAL TRIAL" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">NCCN</data>
      <data key="d8">CLINICAL TRIAL</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">NCCN (National Comprehensive Cancer Network) provides guidance and resources regarding clinical trials across multiple cancer types. For primary CNS lymphoma, NCCN experts recommend that all patients consider joining a clinical trial as part of their treatment approach. NCCN offers patient guidelines and cancer center information designed to help patients find and understand clinical trials. Additionally, NCCN's patient education materials list clinical trials as a treatment option for bladder cancer, noting that patients can join a clinical trial at any time during their care. Through these various resources, NCCN highlights clinical trials as an accessible and important treatment pathway for patients.</data>
      <data key="d12">NCCN</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NCCN" target="CLINICAL TRIALS" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">NCCN</data>
      <data key="d8">CLINICAL TRIALS</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">NCCN patient guidelines cover clinical trials and encourage patients to ask their care team about access to clinical trials. NCCN patient guide provides information about cancer care and encourages patients to consider asking their care team about access to clinical trials</data>
      <data key="d12">NCCN</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NCCN" target="GENETIC COUNSELOR" id="related_to">
