    <edge source="NCCN" target="RECTAL CANCER" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">NCCN</data>
      <data key="d8">RECTAL CANCER</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">NCCN, the National Comprehensive Cancer Network, publishes patient-focused resources on rectal cancer. Specifically, NCCN makes available the NCCN Guidelines for Patients: Rectal Cancer, which are designed to provide patients with reliable, evidence-based information about the disease and its management. These guidelines translate the clinical NCCN Guidelines into plain language so that patients and caregivers can better understand rectal cancer treatment options, decision-making, and care planning. The publication is part of NCCN's broader mission to improve the quality and effectiveness of cancer care by ensuring patients have access to clear, expert-derived guidance. In summary, the entity NCCN is the publisher, and its patient guideline dedicated to rectal cancer is a key resource available to affected individuals and their families.</data>
      <data key="d12">RECTAL CANCER</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NCCN" target="FERTILITY PRESERVATION" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">NCCN</data>
      <data key="d8">FERTILITY PRESERVATION</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">The National Comprehensive Cancer Network (NCCN) provides accessible information on fertility preservation, particularly for adolescents and young adults affected by cancer. This guidance is available through multiple platforms, including the official NCCN.org website and the NCCN Patient Guides for Cancer app. NCCNs patient guidelines and the mobile app are key resources that offer detailed information on fertility preservation for cancer patients, helping individuals understand their options before, during, and after treatment. The organization emphasizes fertility preservation as an important aspect of cancer care, ensuring that patients and families have the knowledge needed to make informed decisions.</data>
      <data key="d12">FERTILITY PRESERVATION</data>
    </edge>
