      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">NCCN is an organization that publishes clinical guidelines and provides resources related to cancer care. Among its resources is the NCCN Cancer Centers network, which consists of cancer centers affiliated with NCCN. These NCCN Cancer Centers are listed on the NCCN website, specifically at NCCN.org/cancercenters, and serve as a clinical trial resource. The list is designed to help patients and providers find cancer centers and available clinical trials in the United States. NCCN Cancer Centers are therefore an integral part of NCCNs effort to connect individuals with cancer treatment and research opportunities, while NCCN itself is recognized for its clinical guidelines and its role in maintaining this network of affiliated cancer centers.</data>
      <data key="d12">NCCN</data>
    </edge>
