    <edge source="CANCER TREATMENT" target="GENETIC TESTING" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">CANCER TREATMENT</data>
      <data key="d8">GENETIC TESTING</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">Genetic testing results may guide cancer treatment</data>
      <data key="d12">GENETIC TESTING</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CANCER TREATMENT" target="CHEMOTHERAPY" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">CANCER TREATMENT</data>
      <data key="d8">CHEMOTHERAPY</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">Chemotherapy is a type of cancer treatment and one component of the broader category of cancer treatment. It is used to combat cancer but can have side effects, notably affecting fertility. Thus, while chemotherapy is a key part of cancer treatment, it is not the entirety of it, and its impact on fertility is an important consideration for patients.</data>
      <data key="d12">CANCER TREATMENT</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CANCER TREATMENT" target="OVARIAN CANCER" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">CANCER TREATMENT</data>
      <data key="d8">OVARIAN CANCER</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">The guide describes treatment recommendations for ovarian cancer as a cancer treatment process.</data>
      <data key="d12">OVARIAN CANCER</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CANCER TREATMENT" target="TREATMENT TEAM" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">CANCER TREATMENT</data>
      <data key="d8">TREATMENT TEAM</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">The treatment team provides and coordinates cancer care, including distress screening as part of cancer care.</data>
      <data key="d12">CANCER TREATMENT</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CANCER TREATMENT" target="FERTILITY PRESERVATION" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">CANCER TREATMENT</data>
      <data key="d8">FERTILITY PRESERVATION</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">Fertility preservation is an important consideration for individuals who are about to begin cancer treatment. It should be considered and planned before starting cancer treatment, as cancer therapies such as chemotherapy, radiation, or surgery may affect fertility. Therefore, fertility preservation should be addressed prior to the initiation of cancer treatment to allow for the best possible options and outcomes. In summary, both consideration and planning for fertility preservation should occur before starting cancer treatment.</data>
      <data key="d12">FERTILITY PRESERVATION</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CANCER TREATMENT" target="PREVENTING PREGNANCY DURING TREATMENT" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">CANCER TREATMENT</data>
      <data key="d8">PREVENTING PREGNANCY DURING TREATMENT</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">Preventing pregnancy during treatment is important because cancer treatment can damage sperm and ovaries.</data>
      <data key="d12">PREVENTING PREGNANCY DURING TREATMENT</data>
    </edge>
