    <edge source="GENERAL HEALTH TESTS" target="FAMILY HISTORY" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">GENERAL HEALTH TESTS</data>
      <data key="d8">FAMILY HISTORY</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">General health tests include family history</data>
      <data key="d12">FAMILY HISTORY</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GENERAL HEALTH TESTS" target="MEDICAL HISTORY" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">GENERAL HEALTH TESTS</data>
      <data key="d8">MEDICAL HISTORY</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">General health tests encompass a range of evaluations used to assess an individual's overall well-being, and they include the medical history as a fundamental component. Specifically, the medical history is recognized as one of the key general health tests, meaning it is an integral part of the initial health assessment process. Beyond simply being a component, the medical history plays a crucial role in guiding clinical decision-making: it helps determine which additional tests and treatments are relevant and appropriate for the individual. In this way, the medical history both serves as a foundational element of general health testing and shapes the subsequent course of care based on the patient's unique background, prior conditions, and risk factors.</data>
      <data key="d12">MEDICAL HISTORY</data>
    </edge>
