    <edge source="SYSTEMIC THERAPY" target="IMMUNOTHERAPY" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">SYSTEMIC THERAPY</data>
      <data key="d8">IMMUNOTHERAPY</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">Immunotherapy is a type of systemic therapy, meaning it is administered throughout the body rather than targeting a single localized area. As a systemic therapy, immunotherapy works by leveraging the bodys immune system to fight cancer. Specifically, it increases immune activity to help identify and destroy cancer cells. Thus, within the broader category of systemic therapy, immunotherapy is distinguished by its mechanism of enhancing the immune response to combat malignancy.</data>
      <data key="d12">SYSTEMIC THERAPY</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SYSTEMIC THERAPY" target="TARGETED THERAPY" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">SYSTEMIC THERAPY</data>
      <data key="d8">TARGETED THERAPY</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">Targeted therapy is a type of systemic therapy, meaning it is a systemic treatment that travels throughout the body to reach cancer cells. However, unlike broader systemic treatments, targeted therapy specifically attacks cancer cells by focusing on specific molecules or pathways involved in tumor growth and survival. While both SYSTEMIC THERAPY and TARGETED THERAPY are related, targeted therapy is categorized under the broader umbrella of systemic therapy, which encompasses treatments that affect the whole body rather than a localized area. Thus, TARGETED THERAPY is a specialized form of SYSTEMIC THERAPY that aims to precisely target cancer cells while distinguishing them from normal cells.</data>
      <data key="d12">TARGETED THERAPY</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SYSTEMIC THERAPY" target="CANCER TREATMENT" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">SYSTEMIC THERAPY</data>
      <data key="d8">CANCER TREATMENT</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">Systemic therapy is a type of cancer treatment using medicines that travel through the bloodstream.</data>
      <data key="d12">CANCER TREATMENT</data>
    </edge>
