      <data key="d8">PFIZER INC.</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">Pfizer Inc. is a corporate supporter acknowledged by the NCCN Foundation for helping to make available the NCCN Guidelines for Patients.
Pfizer Inc. is a corporate supporter acknowledged by the NCCN Foundation for helping make the NCCN Guidelines for Patients available.</data>
      <data key="d12">PFIZER INC.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CANCER INFORMATION SERVICE" target="CLINICAL TRIAL" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">CANCER INFORMATION SERVICE</data>
      <data key="d8">CLINICAL TRIAL</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">The Cancer Information Service assists individuals in locating appropriate clinical trials, including providing guidance on how to find them. It also answers cancer-related questions and addresses specific inquiries about clinical trials, such as their purpose, procedures, and eligibility. Additionally, the service offers contact information for further assistance, ensuring that individuals have access to the support they need when seeking information about cancer and clinical trial participation.</data>
      <data key="d12">CANCER INFORMATION SERVICE</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ANAL CANCER FOUNDATION" target="PEER-TO-PEER SUPPORT PROGRAM" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">ANAL CANCER FOUNDATION</data>
      <data key="d8">PEER-TO-PEER SUPPORT PROGRAM</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">The Anal Cancer Foundation runs the Peer-To-Peer Support Program and provides contact for matching patients/caregivers with peer volunteers; The Anal Cancer Foundation runs and offers the Peer-To-Peer Support Program</data>
      <data key="d12">PEER-TO-PEER SUPPORT PROGRAM</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NATIONAL COMPREHENSIVE CANCER NETWORK" target="NCCN FOUNDATION" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">NATIONAL COMPREHENSIVE CANCER NETWORK</data>
      <data key="d8">NCCN FOUNDATION</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">The NCCN Foundation funds and distributes the NCCN Guidelines for Patients, which are developed, updated, and hosted independently by the National Comprehensive Cancer Network.</data>
      <data key="d12">NCCN FOUNDATION</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NATIONAL COMPREHENSIVE CANCER NETWORK" target="ACUTE LYMPHOBLASTIC LEUKEMIA" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">NATIONAL COMPREHENSIVE CANCER NETWORK</data>
      <data key="d8">ACUTE LYMPHOBLASTIC LEUKEMIA</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">The National Comprehensive Cancer Network (NCCN) publishes patient care guidelines specifically for Acute Lymphoblastic Leukemia (ALL). These NCCN Guidelines for Patients provide comprehensive information about ALL, including details on testing, treatment options, and supportive care.</data>
      <data key="d12">ACUTE LYMPHOBLASTIC LEUKEMIA</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NATIONAL COMPREHENSIVE CANCER NETWORK" target="BPDCN" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">NATIONAL COMPREHENSIVE CANCER NETWORK</data>
      <data key="d8">BPDCN</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">The National Comprehensive Cancer Network (NCCN) is a professional organization that develops clinical practice guidelines for cancer care. Among its resources, the NCCN Guidelines for Patients include a dedicated chapter addressing the treatment of BPDCNblastic plasmacytoid dendritic cell neoplasm, a rare and aggressive blood cancer. This chapter is part of the NCCN's patient-focused educational materials, which are designed to help patients understand their diagnosis and treatment options. The NCCN's coverage of BPDCN in its patient guidelines reflects the organization's commitment to providing up-to-date, evidence-based information for both clinicians and patients. The inclusion of this chapter ensures that individuals affected by BPDCN have accessible guidance on available therapeutic approaches, as outlined by the NCCN's expert panel. Thus, the NCCN directly supports patient education and informed decision-making for BPDCN through this specific chapter in its guidelines.</data>
      <data key="d12">BPDCN</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NATIONAL COMPREHENSIVE CANCER NETWORK" target="BCR::ABL1-POSITIVE B-ALL" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">NATIONAL COMPREHENSIVE CANCER NETWORK</data>
      <data key="d8">BCR::ABL1-POSITIVE B-ALL</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">The National Comprehensive Cancer Network (NCCN) provides clinical guidance that includes a dedicated chapter on the treatment of BCR::ABL1-positive B-ALL. This information is presented in the NCCN Guidelines for Patients, which specifically address management and treatment options for this subtype of acute lymphoblastic leukemia.</data>
      <data key="d12">BCR::ABL1-POSITIVE B-ALL</data>
    </edge>
