      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">Pfizer Inc. supports the availability of the NCCN Guidelines for Patients, while the National Comprehensive Cancer Network independently adapts, updates, and hosts those guidelines.
Pfizer Inc. supports the NCCN Guidelines for Patients, which are independently adapted, updated, and hosted by the National Comprehensive Cancer Network.</data>
      <data key="d12">PFIZER INC.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="UNITED STATES" target="CLINICAL TRIAL" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">UNITED STATES</data>
      <data key="d8">CLINICAL TRIAL</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">In the United States, clinical trials are widely available to patients, and a range of U.S.-specific resources exist to help individuals locate and access these research opportunities. These resources include NCCN Cancer Centers and the National Cancer Institute, which provide listings and guidance for clinical trials across the country. Together, the United States and its clinical trial infrastructure support patient access to studies through centralized and institutional channels.</data>
      <data key="d12">UNITED STATES</data>
    </edge>
