      <data key="d8">FERTILITY-SPARING TREATMENT</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">CERVICAL CANCER and FERTILITY-SPARING TREATMENT are directly related in certain clinical situations. Specifically, fertility-sparing treatment may be an option for individuals diagnosed with cervical cancer that is confined to the cervix, meaning the cancer has not spread beyond the cervical region. This applies when the disease is limited to the cervix itself, and such an approach may be considered as a treatment possibility in these early, localized cases.</data>
      <data key="d12">FERTILITY-SPARING TREATMENT</data>
    </edge>
