    <edge source="MYCHART" target="CARE TEAM" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">MYCHART</data>
      <data key="d8">CARE TEAM</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">MyChart is a patient portal that enables patients to communicate with their care team and track appointments. Through MyChart, patients can send messages to their care team; however, portal messages are not immediately seen by the care team, meaning there may be a delay in response. MyChart serves as the primary tool for patients to stay in contact with their care providers and manage their scheduled appointments.</data>
      <data key="d12">MYCHART</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MYCHART" target="PATIENT" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">MYCHART</data>
      <data key="d8">PATIENT</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">MyChart is a patient portal that allows patients to access test results, track appointments, and communicate with their care team. A patient may set up MyChart specifically to track appointments and communicate with their care team, thereby gaining access to these features and maintaining ongoing engagement with their healthcare providers.</data>
      <data key="d12">MYCHART</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MYCHART" target="APPOINTMENTS" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">MYCHART</data>
      <data key="d8">APPOINTMENTS</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">MyChart is a tool that helps the patient keep track of their appointments, providing a convenient way to manage and stay informed about scheduled visits.</data>
      <data key="d12">MYCHART</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MYCHART" target="PHYSICIAN" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">MYCHART</data>
      <data key="d8">PHYSICIAN</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">MyChart (the patient portal) messages are not immediately seen by a physician. Because of this, any urgent concerns should not be sent through MyChart or portal messaging; instead, they should be called directly to triage. Physicians do not monitor MyChart messages in real time, so portal messaging is not appropriate for time-sensitive or urgent medical issues.</data>
      <data key="d12">PHYSICIAN</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MYCHART" target="NURSE" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">MYCHART</data>
      <data key="d8">NURSE</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">MyChart messages are not immediately seen by a nurse. Because portal messages are not monitored in real time, urgent concerns should not be sent through MyChart. Instead, patients should call triage directly for immediate assistance. This ensures that time-sensitive medical issues receive prompt attention.</data>
      <data key="d12">MYCHART</data>
    </edge>
