      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">Laryngoscopy is a medical procedure used to visualize the inside of the larynx (voice box) and nearby structures of the throat. Direct laryngoscopy is a specific type of laryngoscopy. In direct laryngoscopy, the practitioner inserts a rigid or flexible scope directly into the airway to obtain a clear view of the larynx, often for diagnostic or therapeutic purposes. Both descriptions confirm that direct laryngoscopy falls under the broader category of laryngoscopy, making it one of the methods within this diagnostic and interventional technique.</data>
