    </edge>
    <edge source="PATHOLOGIST" target="DOCTOR" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">PATHOLOGIST</data>
      <data key="d8">DOCTOR</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">A pathologist is a doctor who specializes in testing cells and tissue to diagnose disease. This specialist prepares a detailed pathology report based on those laboratory findings. Separately, the doctor who is caring for the patient reviews the pathology report prepared by the pathologist with the patient, explaining the results and their implications. Together, the pathologists diagnostic work and the doctors patient-facing review form a coordinated process: the pathologist identifies and interprets cellular and tissue abnormalities, while the doctor uses that information to guide the patients understanding and subsequent treatment decisions.</data>
      <data key="d12">DOCTOR</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ABDOMINOPERINEAL RESECTION" target="RECTAL CANCER" id="related_to">
